cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use TopVenues, cite the paper whose numbers you use. The tool is
  described in the tools-track paper below; the corpus method and the
  measurements are in the main-track paper listed under references.
  docs/PAPERS.md binds each paper to its release, snapshot and SHA-256.
title: "TopVenues"
abstract: >-
  An executable corpus and research tool for cybersecurity literature reviews:
  a declared venue and year scope, frozen SQLite snapshots identified by
  SHA-256, ranked search, author analytics and review-ready exports.
type: software
